  "conclusion": "Empirical bisection confirms prompt prefill SIMD tile defect at batch sizes >= 32. Hugging Face PyTorch reference correctly extracts expected targets across all prompt lengths and samplers. Under bitnet.cpp: 1. Short prompts < 32 tokens (29 tokens) succeed under both default (b=512) and micro-batched (b=16) prefill (extracting '$500' cleanly; short passes=2/3). 2. Prompts >= 32 tokens under default prefill (b=512) or explicit b>=32 immediately trigger SIMD tile corruption ('\u5907\u4efd', '2 0 3 0...', garbage runs=7). 3. Micro-batching prompts (b=2..16) avoids tile corruption glyphs but degenerates into repetitive loops on long context without factual retrieval (long correct=0/11). 4. Single-token prefill (b=1 oracle) emits immediate [end of text]. Conclusion: Verified-correct factual generation in bitnet.cpp is strictly confined to prompts under 32 tokens (<= 31 tokens). Long-context RAG factual generation cannot safely operate on the current bitnet.cpp runtime."
